Sval: read Sval's per-site fingerprinting choices from their own prefs

A site's fingerprinting choices (fingerprinting protection off, or one of
its exceptions) live in a pref per site under browser.sval.protection.site.,
which settings sync carries. SvalSiteProtections derives the entries they
need and keeps them on the default branch of two Sval prefs, so the entries
are never saved beside the synced store and none can outlive the choice it
came from.

FingerprintingWebCompatService reads them after the granular-overrides
prefs and follows them as it follows those, so a person's own granular
entries stay theirs and a site's choice takes the place of one for the
same site. No chrome API reaches the service's entries: nsIRFPService only
replaces them wholesale, and this service rewrites them whenever its own
prefs or the remote ones change. The granular prefs themselves cannot hold
them unsaved: a default-branch value is hidden by any user value, and a
change to it notifies no observer while one exists (Pref::SetDefaultValue).

